== no token
GET /orders/ord-5003 HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8008

HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized
content-type: application/problem+json
www-authenticate: Bearer resource_metadata="http://127.0.0.1:8008/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource", scope="orders:read"

{
  "type": "https://harbor.example/problems/unauthorized",
  "title": "Unauthorized",
  "status": 401,
  "detail": "no access token"
}

== Rosa's access token, her own order
200 ord-5003 paid customer cus-001

== tokens that must fail
ID token as access token     401  Audience doesn't match
                                  Bearer resource_metadata="http://127.0.0.1:8008/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource", error="invalid_token"
alg none, no signature       401  Unable to find a signing key that matches: "None"
                                  Bearer resource_metadata="http://127.0.0.1:8008/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource", error="invalid_token"
payload edited               401  Signature verification failed
                                  Bearer resource_metadata="http://127.0.0.1:8008/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource", error="invalid_token"

== Sam's order with Rosa's token
GET /orders/ord-5002 HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8008
Authorization: Bearer <JWT 1275 chars>

HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found
content-type: application/problem+json

{
  "type": "https://harbor.example/problems/order-not-found",
  "title": "Order not found",
  "status": 404,
  "detail": "No order with id ord-5002.",
  "instance": "/orders/ord-5002"
}

== an order for another customer
customer_id cus-002          403  customer_id is not the token's customer

== the same order for Rosa herself
201 /orders/ord-5005

== a token with orders:read only tries to cancel
PUT /orders/ord-5003/cancellation HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8008
Authorization: Bearer <JWT 1066 chars>
Content-Type: application/json

HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden
content-type: application/problem+json
www-authenticate: Bearer resource_metadata="http://127.0.0.1:8008/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource", error="insufficient_scope", error_description="PUT /orders/ord-5003/cancellation needs orders:write", scope="orders:write"

{
  "type": "https://harbor.example/problems/forbidden",
  "title": "Forbidden",
  "status": 403,
  "detail": "PUT /orders/ord-5003/cancellation needs orders:write"
}
